<div class="hero">
  <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Weeks in a Year</nav>
  <h1>Weeks in a Year</h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">How many weeks per year — regular year, leap year, work weeks &amp; school weeks</p>
</div>

<div class="calc-wrap">
  <div class="calc-left">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="quick-answer">
        <span class="qa-big">52 weeks in a year</span>
        <span class="qa-sub">Regular year: 52 weeks + 1 day · Leap year: 52 weeks + 2 days</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-step">1</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">Select Year Type</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="field-group">
        <label class="field-lbl" for="year-type">Year Type</label>
        <select id="year-type" class="field-select" onchange="calc()">
          <option value="365">Regular Year (365 days)</option>
          <option value="366">Leap Year (366 days)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-step">2</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">Result</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="a-label">Weeks in Year</div>
        <div class="a-value" id="r-weeks">52</div>
        <div class="a-unit">weeks</div>
        <div class="a-sub" id="r-sub">365 days ÷ 7 = 52 weeks + 1 day</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stats-row">
        <div class="stat-box">
          <span class="stat-lbl">Exact Weeks</span>
          <span class="stat-val" id="r-exact">52.143</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-box">
          <span class="stat-lbl">Extra Days</span>
          <span class="stat-val" id="r-extra">1 day</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-box">
          <span class="stat-lbl">Work Weeks (52)</span>
          <span class="stat-val">52 weeks</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-box">
          <span class="stat-lbl">Pay Periods (bi-wk)</span>
          <span class="stat-val">26</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="calc-right">

    <div class="content-card">
      <h2>Weeks in a Year — Full Breakdown</h2>
      <div class="tip-box">
        <span class="tip-icon">📅</span>
        <p><strong>Key fact:</strong> 365 ÷ 7 = 52.142857 weeks. That extra 0.142857 of a week = 1 day. So every regular year has exactly <strong>52 weeks and 1 day</strong>. Leap years have <strong>52 weeks and 2 days</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto">
        <table class="conv-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Period</th><th>Days</th><th>Weeks</th><th>Exact</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1 week</td><td>7</td><td>1</td><td>1.000</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1 month (avg)</td><td>30.44</td><td>≈ 4.3</td><td>4.348</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1 quarter (3 mo)</td><td>91.25</td><td>≈ 13</td><td>13.04</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6 months</td><td>182.5</td><td>≈ 26</td><td>26.07</td></tr>
            <tr class="hl"><td><strong>Regular year</strong></td><td><strong>365</strong></td><td><strong>52 + 1 day</strong></td><td><strong>52.143</strong></td></tr>
            <tr class="hl"><td><strong>Leap year</strong></td><td><strong>366</strong></td><td><strong>52 + 2 days</strong></td><td><strong>52.286</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 years</td><td>730</td><td>104 + 2 days</td><td>104.286</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4 years (1 leap)</td><td>1,461</td><td>208 + 5 days</td><td>208.714</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10 years</td><td>3,652</td><td>521 + 5 days</td><td>521.714</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
      <h2>Work Weeks, Pay Periods &amp; School Weeks</h2>
      <div class="use-grid">
        <div class="use-card">
          <div class="use-title">Work Weeks</div>
          <p>A full work year = 52 weeks × 40 hours = <strong>2,080 work hours</strong>. After 10 federal holidays + 10 vacation days (standard US), actual work weeks ≈ 50. Full-time salary ÷ 2,080 = exact hourly rate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="use-card" style="border-left-color:#10b981">
          <div class="use-title" style="color:#059669">Biweekly Pay Periods</div>
          <p>52 weeks ÷ 2 = <strong>26 pay periods</strong> per year. Some years produce 27 biweekly periods depending on the payroll start date — this happens roughly every 11 years per company. Monthly pay = 12 periods/year.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="use-card" style="border-left-color:#f59e0b">
          <div class="use-title" style="color:#d97706">School Weeks</div>
          <p>US school year = <strong>36 weeks</strong> (180 days ÷ 5). Runs September → June. The remaining <strong>16 weeks</strong> are summer (≈10 wks), winter break (2 wks), spring break (1 wk), and other holidays.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="use-card" style="border-left-color:#8b5cf6">
          <div class="use-title" style="color:#7c3aed">ISO Week Numbering</div>
          <p>The ISO 8601 standard numbers weeks 1–52 (sometimes 53). Week 1 = the week containing the year's first Thursday. Some years get a "Week 53" when Jan 1 falls on a Thursday (regular year) or Wed/Thu (leap year).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
      <h2>Upcoming Leap Years</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto">
        <table class="conv-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Year</th><th>Type</th><th>Weeks</th><th>Days</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>2025</td><td>Regular</td><td>52 + 1 day</td><td>365</td></tr>
            <tr class="hl"><td><strong>2026</strong></td><td>Regular</td><td>52 + 1 day</td><td>365</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2027</td><td>Regular</td><td>52 + 1 day</td><td>365</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2028</td><td>Leap Year</td><td>52 + 2 days</td><td>366</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2029</td><td>Regular</td><td>52 + 1 day</td><td>365</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2030</td><td>Regular</td><td>52 + 1 day</td><td>365</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2031</td><td>Regular</td><td>52 + 1 day</td><td>365</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2032</td><td>Leap Year</td><td>52 + 2 days</td><td>366</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2036</td><td>Leap Year</td><td>52 + 2 days</td><td>366</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2040</td><td>Leap Year</td><td>52 + 2 days</td><td>366</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How many weeks in a year?</h3>
        <p>A regular year has <strong>52 weeks and 1 day</strong> (365 ÷ 7 = 52.142857). A leap year has <strong>52 weeks and 2 days</strong> (366 ÷ 7 = 52.286). For most practical purposes, the answer is 52 weeks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is there 52 or 53 weeks in a year?</h3>
        <p>There are always 52 full weeks. The extra 1–2 days don't form a full 53rd week. However, the ISO week numbering system can label up to 53 weeks — this happens when January 1 falls on a Thursday in a regular year.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How many work weeks in a year?</h3>
        <p>52 work weeks. After US holidays (10 days) and 2 weeks PTO, most employees work about 50 weeks = 2,000 hours. The official IRS/HR standard for full-time work is 2,080 hours/year (52 × 40).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How many weeks in a leap year?</h3>
        <p>52 weeks and 2 extra days (366 ÷ 7 = 52.286 weeks). Leap years: 2024, 2028, 2032, 2036. A year is a leap year if divisible by 4, except century years must also be divisible by 400.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How many biweekly pay periods in a year?</h3>
        <p>Usually <strong>26</strong> (52 ÷ 2). Some years have 27 biweekly periods depending on when January 1 falls in the pay cycle. Employers budget 26 pay periods annually but occasionally face a 27-period year.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How many school weeks in a year?</h3>
        <p><strong>36 weeks</strong> in a US school year (180 required school days ÷ 5 days/week). The remaining 16 weeks are vacation: summer (~10 weeks), winter (~2 weeks), spring (~1 week), and other breaks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
      <h2>Related Time Tools</h2>
      <div class="next-grid">
        <a href="/hours-in-a-year" class="next-card">
          <span class="next-tag">Time</span>
          <h3>Hours in a Year</h3>
          <p>8,760 hours in a regular year — work hours and breakdown</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/minutes-in-a-day" class="next-card">
          <span class="next-tag">Time</span>
          <h3>Minutes in a Day</h3>
          <p>1,440 minutes per day — full time unit reference</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/seconds-in-a-year" class="next-card">
          <span class="next-tag">Time</span>
          <h3>Seconds in a Year</h3>
          <p>31,536,000 seconds in a year — exactly calculated</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/hours-in-a-month" class="next-card">
          <span class="next-tag">Time</span>
          <h3>Hours in a Month</h3>
          <p>730 average hours per month — every month covered</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/days-from-today" class="next-card">
          <span class="next-tag">Date</span>
          <h3>Days From Today</h3>
          <p>Find the exact date any number of days from today</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/time-to-decimal-calculator" class="next-card">
          <span class="next-tag">Time</span>
          <h3>Time to Decimal</h3>
          <p>Convert hours &amp; minutes to decimal for timesheets</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline>
function calc() {
  var days = parseInt(document.getElementById('year-type').value);
  var weeks = Math.floor(days / 7);
  var extra = days % 7;
  var exact = (days / 7).toFixed(3);
  document.getElementById('r-weeks').textContent = weeks;
  document.getElementById('r-exact').textContent = exact;
  document.getElementById('r-extra').textContent = extra + (extra === 1 ? ' day' : ' days');
  document.getElementById('r-sub').textContent = days + ' days ÷ 7 = ' + weeks + ' weeks + ' + extra + (extra === 1 ? ' day' : ' days');
}
calc();
</script>
</Layout>
